## Conclusion

RESQAI evolved from a simple idea of classifying disaster tweets into a hybrid AI-assisted humanitarian information-processing system.

The project began with understanding the disaster-information problem, moved through dataset preparation and traditional machine-learning baselines, and then progressed to transformer-based experimentation with DistilBERT and BERTweet. After multiple iterations and training adjustments, BERTweet achieved **78.67% test accuracy and 78.27% weighted F1**.

The remaining limitations motivated the addition of a confidence-based Gemini layer for contextual analysis. The final architecture therefore combines the speed and domain-specific classification of BERTweet with the contextual capabilities of an LLM.

The project demonstrated that errors and failed experiments are not separate from the development process; they are an important part of reaching the final system.
